  "published": "2026-09-19T18:49:42.107Z",
  "releaseNotes": "* Client: arrays of INT, WORD, DINT, DWORD, REAL, LINT and LWORD larger than the PDU are split correctly (failed before)\n      * Client: new tag types li (LINT), si (SINT), ws (WSTRING), wc (WCHAR); lw (LWORD) and WSTRING work\n      * Client: messages larger than the TPDU size are fragmented and reassembled\n      * Client: reconnect works after a connection broke during a fragmented message\n      * Client: alarm updates are registered again after a reconnect\n      * Server: uses the negotiated PDU size and rejects larger jobs with error class 0x85 like a PLC\n      * Every read and write that worked with 2.2.7 sends the same requests as before\n      * see CHANGELOG.md for details",
